---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={"Products Overview | Roos Instruments"}
  description={"Cassini is a modular architecture with Test Instrument Modules provide the building blocks \n\tfor a configurable microwave system with resource ports designed to integrate seamlessly, creating a flexible instrument architecture. \n\tThis gives Cassini drop in measurement capability and frequency extension as well as multi-site expansion."}
  active={["nav-products"]}>
			<!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - START
    =========================== -->
			<section class="breadcrumb-wrapper">
				<div class="container">
					<h2>Products</h2>
					<ol class="breadcrumb">
						<li><a href="/index.html">Home</a></li>
						<li class="active">Products</li>
					</ol>
				</div>
			</section>
			<!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - END
    =========================== -->

			<section id="content" class="roosC container">
				<img title="Modular Microwave" alt="Modular Microwave" src="images/Prod1.png">
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-10 col-sm-offset-1">
						<h2>Modular Microwave</h2>
						<p class="main">
							Cassini isn’t just modular instruments, it’s a modular architecture and there’s a
							difference. Test Instrument Modules provide the building blocks for a configurable microwave
							system with resource ports designed to integrate seamlessly, creating a flexible instrument
							architecture. This gives Cassini drop in measurement capability and frequency extension as
							well as instant multi-site expansion.
						</p>
						<a href="core.html" title="System Core">How it all works &raquo;</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="row">
					<!-- TODO: Replace next 4 .png with proper svg-->
					<div class="col-sm-2 col-sm-offset-1">
						<img src="images/mod_src.png" alt="Source Icon">
					</div>
					<div class="col-sm-8">
						<h3>Sources</h3>
						<p class="main">Precision microwave signal delivery. Continuous wave signals from 100MHz to
							20 GHz. Modulated sources from 10kHz to 6GHz carrier with 20MHz baseband.</p>
						<a href="core.html#Sourcing" title="System Core">Learn More &raquo;</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-2 col-sm-offset-1">
						<img src="images/mod_comb.png" alt="Combiner Icon">
					</div>
					<div class="col-sm-8">
						<h3>Signal Combination</h3>
						<p class="main">These instruments extend the capability of microwave sources by providing
							signal routing and signal conditioning features. Two input sources can be routed out of
							4 different outputs for increased port efficiency. Built-in step attenuators and
							amplifications extends the dynamic range of traditional sources providing 150dB of
							adjustable dynamic range. Precision microwave combiners enable two-tone signal delivery
							for high performance intermodulation and linearity test setups.</p>
						<a href="core.html#Combination" title="Signal Combination">Learn More &raquo;</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-2 col-sm-offset-1">
						<img src="images/mod_rec.png" alt="Receiver Icon">
					</div>
					<div class="col-sm-8">
						<h3>Receiver</h3>
						<p class="main">
							The hub for all measurements on Cassini, the synchrodoyne vector receiver provides two
							direct measure ports for 100MHz to 20 GHz signals and a dedicated low frequency port for
							signals from 100kHz to 2 GHz. The local oscillator can be shared with up to three
							different frequency converting testsets along with their corresponding downconverted IF
							signals to provide cross-instrument, phase-coherent measurements.
						</p>
						<a href="core.html#Reciever" title="Receiver">Learn More &raquo;</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-2 col-sm-offset-1">
						<img src="images/mod_ts.png" alt="Testset Icon">
					</div>
					<div class="col-sm-8">
						<h3>Test Sets</h3>
						<p class="main">Cassini Test Sets integrate with the RF System Core source to extend source and
							receiver test ports. These specialized front-ends provide path switching, signal
							conditioning, source combining, and frequency conversion for single insertion
							intermodulation, linearity, VNA, spectrum analysis, noise figure and power meter
							measurements.</p>
						<a href="testsets.html" title="Test Sets">Learn More &raquo;</a>
					</div>

				</div>
				<hr class="space">
				<hr class="space">

				<img title="System Integration" alt="System Integration" src="images/Prod2.png">
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-10 col-sm-offset-1">
						<h2>System Integration</h2>
						<p class="main">
							A truly unique aspect of Cassini ATE is the configurable system integration layer. Moving
							this
							traditional fixed layer into the device interface environment allows the test system’s
							architecture to be dynamically configured for each device application. interchangeable
							blind-mate interface blocks allow any instrument in any position on
							the test head to optimzie for signal layout, multi-site, and forward/backward compatibility.
							Coaxial micorwave cables and conformable waveguide combine high performance signal delivery
							and
							cost effective
							routing.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<hr class="space">
				<hr class="space">

				<img title="System Integration" alt="System Integration" src="images/Prod3.png">
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-10 col-sm-offset-1">
						<h2>Port & Frequency Extension</h2>
						<p class="main">
							Cassini Test Sets integrate with the RF System Core to extend source and vector receiver
							test ports. These specialized front-ends provide full vector corrected path switching,
							signal conditioning, source combining, and frequency conversion for signle insertion
							intermodulation, linearity, VNA, spectrum analysis, continuous, pulsed, noise figure and
							power meter tests. <a href="testsets.html">Learn More &raquo;</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<style is:inline>
					.roosC abc {
						color: #777 !important;
					}
				</style>
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-2 col-sm-offset-1" style="padding: 0 30px;">
						<a href="pdf/RI8545_TestSet_20GHz.pdf" title="RI8545 TestSet 20 GHz" target="_blank">
							<img title="RI8545 20 GHz TestSet" alt="RI8545 20 GHz TestSet" src="images/ri8545_tim.png">
							<h4>RI8545</h4>
							<div style="width: 100%; border: 2px solid #324993; margin-bottom: 10px;"></div>
						</a>
						<p>0.1 to 20 GHz</p>
						<p>4 Vector Tx/Rx</p>
					</div>

					<div class="col-sm-2" style="padding: 0 30px;">
						<a href="pdf/RI8607_TestSet_50GHz.pdf" title="RI8607 TestSet 2-50 GHz" target="_blank">
							<img title="RI8607 TestSet 4-50 GHz" alt="RI8607 TestSet 2-50 GHz"
								src="images/ri8563_tim.png">
							<h4>RI8607 </h4>
							<div style="width: 100%; border: 2px solid #BD1A8D; margin-bottom: 10px;"></div>
						</a>
						<p>2 to 50 GHz</p>
						<p>2 Vector Tx/Rx</p>
					</div>

					<div class="col-sm-2" style="padding: 0 30px;">
						<a href="pdf/RI8580_TestSet_60GHz.pdf" title="RI8580 TestSet 60 GHz" target="_blank">
							<img title="RI8580 60 GHz TestSet" alt="RI8580 60 GHz TestSet" src="images/ri8580_tim.png">
							<h4>RI8580 </h4>
							<div style="width: 100%; border: 2px solid #EA2D49; margin-bottom: 10px;"></div>
						</a>
						<p>50 to 70 GHz</p>
						<p>1 Vector Tx/Rx</p>
						<p>1 Scalar Rx</p>
					</div>

					<div class="col-sm-2" style="padding: 0 30px;">
						<a href="pdf/RI8604_TestSet_80GHz.pdf" title="RI8604 TestSet 80 GHz" target="_blank">
							<img title="RI8604 80 GHz TestSet" alt="RI8604 60 GHz TestSet" src="images/ri8604_tim.png">
							<h4>RI8604</h4>
							<div style="width: 100%; border: 2px solid #F5811F; margin-bottom: 10px;"></div>
						</a>
						<p>71 to 86 GHz</p>
						<p>1 Vector Tx/Rx</p>
						<p>1 Scalar Rx</p>
					</div>

					<div class="col-sm-2" style="padding: 0 30px;">
						<a href="#" title="RI8610 100 GHz TestSet" target="_blank">
							<img title="RI8610 100 GHz TestSet" alt="RI8610 100 GHz TestSet"
								src="images/ri8604_tim.png">
							<h4>RI8610 </h4>
							<div style="width: 100%; border: 2px solid #f56e1f; margin-bottom: 10px;"></div>
						</a>
						<p>86 to 110 GHz</p>
						<p>1 Vector Tx/Rx</p>
						<p>1 Scalar Rx</p>
					</div>
					<hr class="space">
					<p class="main"><br>Select an instrument above or <a href="/tims.html#testsets">Browse All TIMs
							&raquo;</a>
					</p>
				</div>


				<hr class="space">
				<div class="row">
					<img style="width: 100%" title="Ultimate Flexibility" alt="Ultimate Flexibility"
						src="images/Image 26.png">
				</div>
				<div class="row roosC">
					<div class="col-sm-8 col-sm-offset-2">
						<h3>Multi-Instrument Signal Flow</h3>
						<p>When all of the pieces come together, the end result is a complete microwave test
							system with unparalleled flexibility and resource efficiency. With both instrument-level
							calibrations and a system-wide vector calibrfation that incorporates the integration layer,
							Cassini delivers true virtual VNA, spectrum analyzer, and power meter measurement
							capability. The multi-layered calibration guarantees accurate and repeatable source and
							measurement capability right to the test port.
						</p>
						<p><a href="testsets.html">Learn More &raquo;</a></p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<hr class="space">
				<hr class="space">
			</section> <!-- End of #content section-->
</Base>
